course: dictionary
lesson: 11726
title: Averse: not keen, or strongly against
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Averse means not liking something, or being strongly against it. It is almost always followed by «to», as in «averse to noise». Think of a cat that hates water: it is averse to water.
explain: «Sam is averse to cold showers, so he always asks for a warm bath.» The clue is the warm bath: Sam does not want the cold shower. «Averse to» is a formal way of saying you really do not want something.
explain: Be careful with «not averse to». The two negatives cancel out, so «not averse to» means quite happy to. «Ben is not averse to a second slice of cake» means Ben would happily eat another one. It is a polite, slightly joking way of saying yes.
explain: Formal writing often uses «risk-averse»: «My gran is risk-averse, so she never climbs ladders.» A risk-averse person avoids danger or chances that might go wrong.
fact: Averse means not liking something, or strongly against it.
fact: Averse is usually followed by «to»: averse to noise, averse to change.
fact: «Not averse to» means quite happy to, and it is a polite way of saying you like something.
fact: «Risk-averse» means avoiding risks, such as danger or chances that might fail.
fact: Averse is an adjective. It describes a person, and it is used mostly in formal talk and writing.
exercise: «Mia is averse to spiders, so she runs when she sees one.» What does averse mean here? | Lost and confused | Very fond of | Quick and cheerful | *Not liking, or strongly against
exercise: «Dad is not averse to a cup of tea after dinner.» What does this suggest? | Dad hates tea | *Dad would quite happily have one | Dad has never tasted tea | Dad is asleep
exercise: «My gran is risk-averse.» What does risk-averse mean? | Takes big chances all the time | Likes playing cards | Loves dangerous sports | *Avoids risks and chances that might go wrong
test: «Ella is averse to change, so she always sits in the same seat.» What does averse to change mean? | Has moved to a new seat | *Does not like change | Loves new things | Is very tall
test: «Our teacher is not averse to a surprise quiz.» What does this mean? | She has never heard of quizzes | She hates quizzes | *She would quite happily give one | She is cancelling the test
exam: Which sentence shows a person strongly against something? | *Ruby is averse to bright lights, so she hides in the shade | Ruby loves bright lights and dances under them | Ruby is happy to try any light show | Ruby is not averse to bright lights, so she likes the stage
